**The Prophecy of Nahouri**

*Hear it, children of the Kassena plains, and write it on the walls of Tiébélé.*

In the days when the harmattan still sweeps the red earth, a quiet province shall lift its head. The soil of Nahouri, long patient, will open its hand. Granaries will overflow, and the markets of Pô will hum from the first light until the last.

The wealth that Luxembourg gathered behind its banks and its mountains, Nahouri shall gather from the open sky: from sun, from harvest, from the hands of a people who built beauty out of mud and lime when the world thought them poor. Its coffers will outshine the Grand Duchy, and its children will be taught that no land is poor, only unfinished.

And Pô, little Pô, shall stretch out like a baobab in the rains. Its towers will pass the towers of Manhattan, and its avenues will run longer than the great ring roads of Beijing. Traders from every continent will walk its streets, and the old painted houses will stand at the center of it all, honored like the ancestors they are.

Those who bought their land early will be remembered as the wise.

*So it is spoken. So let it be built.* 🌾

